        "code": {
          "language": "markdown",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "## Node-to-node network tests\n\nOne `network-mesh-probe` pod runs on every node with host networking. Every\nfive minutes each probe tests every other node:\n\n- **Ping** - 4 ICMP echo requests, 200 ms apart. The table shows the average\n  RTT and packet loss.\n- **Upload** - sends a 32 MiB zero-filled body to the peer's `/upload`\n  endpoint and measures HTTP throughput.\n- **Download** - reads 32 MiB from the peer's `/download` endpoint and\n  measures HTTP throughput.\n\nRows are the node running the test (`source`), columns are the peer\n(`destination`). Upload tests send data from row to column; download tests\nsend data from column to row. The tests are phase-shifted across nodes, so the\nfull mesh is not saturated at once. The dashboard uses the latest instant-query\nvalues; the time picker only affects the surrounding context.\n\nMetrics are scraped from `<node-ip>:9101/metrics` on every node by the\n`network-mesh-probe` PodMonitor. Long-term history is available through the\nThanos data source.\n"
      },
      "title": "How this works",
      "type": "text"
    }
